-- **The warning silenced by listing it** (MS11 phase 307, `~f8x53`, his ruling
-- of 2026-11-10). `PassesNothingOwn.thena` is the same shape and warns: its
-- header says `exporting ( )` while a `public import` hands `Bit` on. This file
-- names `Bit` in its own clause, so the header enumerates everything the file
-- offers and nothing is said. **The clunkiness is the point** — `Bit` is
-- `Guarded`'s namespace and not this file's.
module test.modules.ListsWhatTravels exporting ( Bit mine ) where

public import test.modules.Guarded

mine : Bit.Bit
mine = Bit.off
